The Jacobian matrix of a vector-valued function of several variables is the matrix of all its first-order partial derivatives. 
If this matrix is square, that is, if the number of components of function values, then its determinant is called the Jacobian determinant. 
Both the matrix and the determinant are often referred to simply as the Jacobian. 

Carl Gustav Jacob Jacobi was born of Ashkenazi Jewish parentage in Potsdam. 
Carl was a mathematician who made fundamental contributions to elliptic functions, dynamics, differential equations, determinants and number theory. 
